1
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:04,917
Gold Grotter, the King of the Pirates,

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,977
attained every treasure
that the world had to offer.

3
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:12,766
Smiling, even as he stood upon the scaffold,
he issued a challenge to the world.

4
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,997
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,021
You can have it.

6
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:17,897
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

7
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:19,740
Now you just have to find it.

8
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:25,620
Now those who dare to dream hoist their
flags and sail into the Great Pirate Era.

9
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:04,940
I don't know if you do
it, it's M .I .N .I .N .E.

10
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:09,220
Oh, the only reason i
am is with our rules.

11
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:15,017
No doubt, it's the only part of me.

12
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:16,617
I never have the same life.

13
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:19,817
I can't believe it,
it's the only way i can.

14
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:25,597
But the future is the same.

15
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,357
I can't believe it, it's the same.

16
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,457
I can't believe it, it's the same.

17
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:30,370
I can't believe it, it's the same.

18
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:46,500
We go!

19
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:51,540
We go! No!

20
00:01:58,700 --> 00:01:59,720
Come on.

21
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,100
Just apologize already.

22
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:05,346
Don't you have something
you want to live for?

23
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,060
Well, kid, what you thinking?

24
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:11,920
You screwed up and now it's time to pay.

25
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:13,280
So speak up.

26
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:16,561
Please, take a look at that brat.

27
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:19,152
Obviously you scared him silent, Captain.

28
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:22,797
I can't blame the kid after
that guy with the schnoz

29
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,977
and that chick with the long
hair picked a fight with us.

30
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:26,597
We're in a worse mood than usual.

31
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:31,504
Now if you don't want to be our personal
punching bag, you'd best ask forgiveness!

32
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:35,237
Neil get down in the
dirt forget your pride.

33
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:39,397
Otherwise, you're gonna end up throwing
your life away over some small mistake.

34
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:43,186
After all our captain's trigger
figure can be a little twitchy.

35
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,617
Come on kid just do it
you shouldn't mess around

36
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:51,877
with Straw Hat luffy you're
gonna die if you don't.

37
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:55,697
Do what he says all
right look i'm sorry now

38
00:02:55,780 --> 00:03:00,980
i got somewhere to be
what's wrong with you?

39
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:10,580
Bad move say goodbye punk.

40
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,689
AHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH

41
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:45,830
What happened?

42
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:51,660
Hey, that guy.

43
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:53,056
Did he do something?

44
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,077
Why are you being such an ass about this?

45
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,437
I just want to go fish.

46
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,060
Well, too bad you can't.

47
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,497
Give me one good reason.

48
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:08,557
And while you're at it, give me one good
reason why I should even listen to you.

49
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:11,517
I don't want to hang out
together any more than you do,

50
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:13,306
but I can't let you get lost.

51
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,617
Don't get me wrong, though.

52
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:17,377
Nothing would make me happier
than leaving you here for good.

53
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:18,460
Too bad, huh?

54
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,877
The point is, everyone's
meeting on the ship,

55
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:23,489
so you don't get to go
fishing on your own.

56
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:27,320
What a joke.

57
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:32,957
Number seven thinks he can talk crap
to number one and get away with it.

58
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:35,697
You think you're better than me
just because you got here first?

59
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:38,837
It's not like everyone
swam to Sabaody, all right?

60
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,685
You got nothing to brag about!

61
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:41,810
Sure.

62
00:04:41,893 --> 00:04:42,723
Whatever you say.

63
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:43,960
Number seven.

64
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:46,010
Fine!

65
00:04:46,093 --> 00:04:47,215
You want to fight me?

66
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:51,077
I've trained these legs on the
shores of hell for two years!

67
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:54,925
Then you better use them to run,
because I will cut you in half!

68
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:02,880
Captain Luffy! Aw, man. You okay?

69
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,190
Luffy!

70
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:10,820
Oh my gosh, I missed you guys so much!

71
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,200
It's me!

72
00:05:12,780 --> 00:05:13,880
Hey, Luffy!

73
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,030
Franky!

74
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,070
Nami!

75
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:23,860
Sniper Gang!

76
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,030
Awesome!

77
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:30,397
Oh wow, you sure changed
a lot in two years, huh?

78
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:32,740
I bet you're all super strong now!

79
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:36,085
What are the Straw Hats up to?

80
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,535
They're just sitting.

81
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:38,975
Did something happen?

82
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:40,557
Uh, yeah, but keep it down.

83
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:42,477
They're pissed off, so
don't look them in the eye.

84
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:45,325
You don't want to pick
a fight with these guys.

85
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:47,660
What the hell?

86
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,940
Whoa, what happened, boss?

87
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,600
I was messed up.

88
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:55,660
Like, all of a sudden, I got these chills.

89
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:59,560
Never seen a trick like that before.

90
00:06:00,620 --> 00:06:01,597
Oh, I forgot.

91
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:03,856
But, we got another problem actually.

92
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:08,140
The thing is, Kaku, I mean
Robin, isn't a real pickle.

93
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:12,580
She was kidnapped and
you let the bastards go?

94
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:13,780
Yeah, sorry.

95
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:16,140
I mean it all happened so fast.

96
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:17,977
They must be human traffickers.

97
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:19,257
This could be real bad.

98
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:20,957
They could try to sell her at auction.

99
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:22,746
Like what happened with Kuma?

100
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:26,589
Uh, get a good look, Adam?

101
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:29,740
No, like I said, it
happened all sudden like.

102
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,110
Hey, Captain,

103
00:06:31,193 --> 00:06:34,357
they must have nabbed Kaku because
they thought she was the real Robin.

104
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,499
We might be in over our heads here.

105
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:38,860
I should have known, you're right.

106
00:06:39,020 --> 00:06:41,314
She does look just like the real thing.

107
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,834
Guess that worked against us this time.

108
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:46,956
Hey, are you keeping secrets from me?

109
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:51,880
I don't care. Leave her.

110
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:53,997
It's not our problem if she dies.

111
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:54,910
What?

112
00:06:54,993 --> 00:06:55,823
Okay.

113
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:57,537
Are you nuts?

114
00:06:57,620 --> 00:06:59,620
Luffy, Robin is our friend!

115
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:02,680
Listen, what is this thing?

116
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,100
And why does it talk?

117
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:07,977
If this is supposed to be
a joke, it's not funny!

118
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,531
We lost Robin once, don't care about that!

119
00:07:10,620 --> 00:07:11,797
See, it's doing it again.

120
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,220
It can't be a toy.

121
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:14,700
Take it back, Luffy!

122
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:15,780
Get off of me!

123
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:23,517
Alright, screw this thing with Robin
and screw this stuffed animal thing!

124
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,357
We gotta get our whole team
together here on Crow 46!

125
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,270
And pronto!

126
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:32,260
That punk with the long nose,
that woman with the orange hair,

127
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:35,028
and that crappy kid
with the giant backpack!

128
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:38,258
Hunt them down and kick their asses!

129
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:43,537
We're gonna show the whole damn world what
happens when you cross-Straw Hat Luffy!

130
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:44,560
Uh, Roger!

131
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:48,657
Don't kill him yet so we can make
a good show of it, huh, Captain?

132
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:52,857
We'll drag him through the streets till
everyone on Sabo and he's shaking in fear!

133
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:54,000
Works for me!

134
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:55,517
Are you crazy?!

135
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,430
Cut it out!

136
00:07:56,513 --> 00:07:58,397
It's only been two years.

137
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,577
What happened to you?

138
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:00,717
This is wrong.

139
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,777
I don't know. I'm just.

140
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:04,537
I'm so sad. Right?

141
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:06,477
Now you're making me cry.

142
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,537
For the last time.

143
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:10,277
What is this stupid thing?

144
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,637
And none of you want to help.

145
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,550
Robin.

146
00:08:12,633 --> 00:08:14,157
Nobody's gonna say anything.

147
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:16,797
Why is this runt so attached to us anyway?

148
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:17,857
When we're done here.

149
00:08:17,940 --> 00:08:19,397
Maybe we should try selling it.

150
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,310
Damn it.

151
00:08:20,393 --> 00:08:21,223
Forget this.

152
00:08:21,306 --> 00:08:23,157
I don't have time to argue with you.

153
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,137
I'll save her.

154
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:25,057
You're on my own!

155
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,500
I don't need you!

156
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:32,700
I'm coming, Robin!

157
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:33,760
Hold on!

158
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,000
What was that?

159
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:39,519
They have a fight?

160
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:41,737
I don't know.

161
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:43,291
But it's definitely them.

162
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:46,617
I mean, they haven't aged
well in the past two years.

163
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:49,171
But nobody else has a weird pet like that.

164
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:51,880
Looks like the reports are true after all.

165
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:53,840
They're alive.

166
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:58,331
The Straw Hats are back, and
they're causing trouble again.

167
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:02,620
This is Grove Number 47. It's them.

168
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:05,349
We've sighted six Straw
Hats and their pet.

169
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:13,357
The rumors that they recruited are
the pirates seem to be true as well.

170
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:16,969
They should be assembling on
Grove Number 46 any minute now.

171
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:17,990
Understood.

172
00:09:18,073 --> 00:09:19,517
Then we'd better move quickly.

173
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,317
Evacuate the locals before
this becomes a war zone.

174
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,230
Roger.

175
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:25,460
Pirates are gathering at Grove 46.

176
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:27,357
Our targets are the Straw Hats.

177
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,397
We'll engage them in the Lawless Zone.

178
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:31,200
They may have reinforcements.

179
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:32,897
Block all routes of escape.

180
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:35,920
Close in on them from
Grove 40, 42, and 44.

181
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:37,500
Make it snappy.

182
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:39,820
G1 is sending in backup now.

183
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,398
Sent a matter, sir.

184
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:52,157
I'm heading in first.

185
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:55,660
Pucci and Pucci will accompany me.

186
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,050
Whoa!

187
00:09:57,133 --> 00:09:59,020
You're deploying pacifistas, sir?

188
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:01,120
Of course I am!

189
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:03,940
You fools!

190
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:07,494
Haven't you learned not to
underestimate the Straw Hats?

191
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:10,000
It's been two years since the war.

192
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:13,157
Surely they've only grown
stronger during that time.

193
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:18,064
They may be rookies, but make no mistake,
they're the most dangerous pirates here!

194
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:21,960
As for what happened last time,

195
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:25,277
we were never able to determine why Kuma

196
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:27,948
sent them away instead
of apprehending them.

197
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:32,860
But even after his personality was wiped,

198
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:36,917
his actions seemed to indicate that
they would be returning here someday.

199
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:42,120
And now that they have, we must ensure
this doesn't end like it did two years ago.

200
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,380
Let's move!

201
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,877
To be

202
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:04,180
continued...

203
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:21,700
Sanji! Franky!

204
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:24,420
What happened to them? Why?

205
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:29,200
Robin gets taken away and you don't care?

206
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:33,280
What's wrong with you?

207
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:38,680
I've been working so hard these past
two years to be a better doctor!

208
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,180
But for what?

209
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:45,080
Chopper!

210
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:47,140
Hey!

211
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:52,260
Yoo-hoo, over here!

212
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:55,654
I can tell it was you from a mile away!

213
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:00,240
It's Yasopp!

214
00:12:00,580 --> 00:12:02,280
Jeez, you got so big!

215
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,600
Just look at you!

216
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:06,840
I bet I could even ride
your back, couldn't I?

217
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:07,962
You doing okay?

218
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,620
Oh, so cuddly!

219
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:13,480
I'm sure the Lady
Reindeers just adore you!

220
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:16,880
I missed you, Chopper, so much!

221
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:21,580
Uh, uh, Nami?

222
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:22,700
Uh-huh.

223
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:25,400
Wait a second.

224
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:29,681
I'm happy to see you guys and all,
but now's not the time for this.

225
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:31,427
Robin is in serious trouble.

226
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:37,850
Huh?

227
00:12:37,933 --> 00:12:39,920
They're just pretending to be you?

228
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:42,065
That's why there's two Nami's?

229
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:44,580
Use your head, okay?

230
00:12:44,940 --> 00:12:47,997
Robin was able to avoid the
government for 20 years.

231
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:51,957
Do you really think someone could
just grab her and stuff her in a bag?

232
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,452
No offense, but come on.

233
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:58,660
I see, I have a tough time telling humans
apart, but she didn't even smell right.

234
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:03,516
Darn it, now I'm starting to get mad.

235
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:07,637
If we see one of them again, I'm gonna
punch them in their big fake face.

236
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:10,440
They've got some nerve,
pretending to be us.

237
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:13,581
I mean, why would they do
that in the first place?

238
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:17,297
It's almost like we're
celebrities or something.

239
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:18,420
That's crazy.

240
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:21,160
Hey, don't let it go to your head.

241
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:23,421
Although you aren't that far off,

242
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:27,737
since our captain worked up quite a
reputation for fighting in that war.

243
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:30,173
I have to come up with a cool autograph.

244
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:31,940
I've already got one.

245
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:33,057
Come on, you two.

246
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:35,780
We're famous criminals, not celebrities.

247
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:44,740
Topper, where'd you go?

248
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:46,900
Come back.

249
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:50,742
And he sucks that little
dude was a pet for real.

250
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:52,980
He, like, doubled the credibility.

251
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,100
Oh, my side hurts.

252
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,500
Are you nuts?

253
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:01,137
That talking stuffed animal thing
was part of the real Straw Hat,

254
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:02,573
so you let it get away?

255
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:04,260
Why didn't you tell me?

256
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:06,620
And why are you looking for it?

257
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:11,857
Oh, sure, go look for it like
we have any idea where we went.

258
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:15,457
Yeah, I mean, Sabo Odi is super
big, and that guy was teeny tiny.

259
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:16,497
I can't do this.

260
00:14:16,580 --> 00:14:18,100
I am dying here!

261
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:23,260
Forget running. We'll walk.

262
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:24,460
Power walk.

263
00:14:26,340 --> 00:14:27,420
Hancock was right.

264
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:30,617
With all the pirates around,
this mustache is pretty handy.

265
00:14:30,700 --> 00:14:33,347
I don't want to fight
with those guys anyway.

266
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:37,717
Look, it's that kid with the backpack.

267
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:40,035
Maybe our luck ain't so bad after all.

268
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:44,342
Boss called him a kid, but he kind
of looks like an old man to me.

269
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,920
Oh, it's you guys?

270
00:14:49,420 --> 00:14:52,077
Hey, friend, we need you to come with us!

271
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:54,240
Let's do this nice and quiet, okay?

272
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:58,137
We don't want any trouble You really
pissed off our captain, kiddo?

273
00:14:58,220 --> 00:15:00,514
I'd prepare for the worst if I was you!

274
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,390
What's wrong?

275
00:15:02,473 --> 00:15:04,257
You're so scared you can't even talk?

276
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:06,300
Hey, Sanji, how's it going?

277
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:08,940
And Zoro, too, wow!

278
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:10,900
Long time no see, huh, guys?

279
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:13,420
Too long, right?

280
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:17,440
Yeah, well, let's get going then.

281
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:19,977
You mean the rest of
the crew's here already?

282
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:21,360
Sorry I was so late.

283
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:23,100
Good thing you found me.

284
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:31,180
Well, he knows the Straw
Heads, but we don't know him.

285
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:32,200
Like I care.

286
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:35,285
Just take him to Luffy
and he'll sort this out.

287
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:51,132
Reporting from Grove 46.

288
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:55,297
All the new recruits the Straw
Hats picked up are gathering here.

289
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:58,097
And from the looks of things, I'd say
there might be nearly a hundred of them.

290
00:15:58,180 --> 00:16:01,777
Most of them are nobodies, but
there are four captains at least.

291
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:03,597
I see Gashed Albion for one.

292
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:05,497
He's worth 92 million.

293
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:07,337
Then there's Libserviced Outta.

294
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:08,960
Who's worth 88 million.

295
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:14,720
But those aren't the ones
I'm really worried about.

296
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:17,257
They've also got wet-haired caribou.

297
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:18,977
Worth 210 million.

298
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:20,560
The captain of his crew.

299
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:23,897
He brought his brother with him.

300
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:25,697
Blood-splattered coribou.

301
00:16:25,780 --> 00:16:28,440
His bounty's at 190 million.

302
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:52,020
The Navy is here?

303
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:53,177
So they know.

304
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:56,120
Very well, then. Take it easy! No pushing!

305
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:57,620
We're songs, okay?

306
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:58,917
And we're waiting for you!

307
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,588
I still need a moment more.

308
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:04,838
My fans are calling for an encore,
you see, and I can't let them down.

309
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:08,720
Encore! Encore! Encore! Encore! Encore!

310
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:14,020
I think I owe them this much at
least, so please wait up for me.

311
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:34,467
Those cheese could bring a dead
man back from his grave, baby.

312
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,097
This is the Navy!

313
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:42,180
Nobody move!

314
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,661
What's the deal?

315
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:44,840
That's not cool.

316
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,577
This is the last living
member of the Rumbar Pirates.

317
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:52,484
The Humming Swordsman, Brook, presumed
dead until now with a bounty of 33 million.

318
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:57,227
Despite his skeletal state, our reports
indicate that Soul King is this pirate.

319
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,277
In addition to his previous crimes,

320
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:03,937
we have further information that indicates
he is now working for Straw Hat Luffy.

321
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:05,200
Soul King, Brook!

322
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:07,497
Or rather, Humming Swordsman, Brook!

323
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:09,640
You're under arrest for piracy!

324
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:15,100
No, it can't be true!

325
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:17,600
I feel like my whole life is a lie!

326
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:19,560
He was a pirate all along?

327
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:22,838
But wait, Stryhat Luffy's
been missing for years now.

328
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:26,100
It's been a good run,
Brook, but it's over.

329
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:30,640
Your betrayal's not exactly
a surprise, Mr. Manager.

330
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:34,837
You're the one to blame telling me you
were gonna retire right after the show.

331
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,417
How could you do this to me?

332
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:37,540
A pity,

333
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:41,937
but it seems like I would have been better
off keeping you in that cage after all.

334
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:45,079
We were gonna be rich, but
now our company's ruined.

335
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:47,378
You're nothing but a filthy traitor.

336
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:54,220
If my life's going to hell,
I'm taking you with me.

337
00:18:57,620 --> 00:18:59,260
That is so cool!

338
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:01,960
Heck yeah!

339
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:05,540
Can I get a body like that too?

340
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:18,100
So can you like Transformers stuff,
shoot beams, missiles, laser eyes?

341
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,920
Hurry, show me, show me!

342
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:24,140
I can hear the dreams of men on
my massive metal shoulders. Wow!

343
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:26,380
I'm back and better than ever.

344
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:28,120
I'm not just me.

345
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:32,080
I've armored me, baby!

346
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:35,677
Robot! Robot!

347
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:39,400
I know he's cool, but stop
before you have a heart attack!

348
00:19:42,260 --> 00:19:43,977
One thing's bugging me, though.

349
00:19:44,060 --> 00:19:46,317
Those giant robo-hands
are great for bashing,

350
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,929
but how are you supposed
to do detail work?

351
00:19:50,340 --> 00:19:51,800
Never doubt the master.

352
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:53,210
Whoa!

353
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:54,250
Dude!

354
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:56,087
He's got a hand in his hand!

355
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,450
Oh, my God!

356
00:19:58,160 --> 00:19:58,990
Robin!

357
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:01,770
Nani!

358
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:03,280
I love the hair!

359
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:07,900
Wow, he looks terrible.

360
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,729
Did he do that to himself?

361
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:12,400
It's Franky, don't ask.

362
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,657
Whoa, this must be the coding, huh?

363
00:20:16,740 --> 00:20:18,177
Wanna see something else cool?

364
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:20,200
Press my nose. Your nose?

365
00:20:20,580 --> 00:20:23,168
Press and hold it for
three seconds or more.

366
00:20:24,420 --> 00:20:26,891
Apply pressure to the nasal region, human.

367
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:29,640
Holy crap, he's like a real robot!

368
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:31,110
I'm excited.

369
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:34,620
One, two, three!

370
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:37,240
Wow, he grew hair!

371
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:42,720
Wait a sec, can you style it?

372
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,120
Easy as pie.

373
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:49,640
Hey, look who it is.

374
00:20:49,860 --> 00:20:50,740
What's up?

375
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:52,960
Yeah, I see you.

376
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:56,077
Ugh, like our crew didn't
stick out enough already.

377
00:20:56,160 --> 00:20:58,700
Can I see your new weapons, please? Can I?

378
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:03,720
Sorry buddy,

379
00:21:04,140 --> 00:21:07,617
that's the main event, so we gotta
wait till the captain shows up, Mecha!

380
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:09,100
He made robot noises!

381
00:21:09,380 --> 00:21:11,100
Is Mecha his new catchphrase?

382
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:14,700
Hello there!

383
00:21:15,860 --> 00:21:17,760
Hey Rayleigh! Hey Chaka!

384
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:21,657
Sorry to interrupt your reunion,
but we've kinda got an incident.

385
00:21:21,740 --> 00:21:24,817
Actually, two very large incidents
that demand your attention.

386
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:26,720
Put the guitar down now!

387
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:28,860
Hands in the air, pirate!

388
00:21:29,140 --> 00:21:30,520
There's no escape!

389
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:38,460
Members of the band, my lovely
chorus, this will be my final song.

390
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:40,500
Will you share it with me?

391
00:21:44,140 --> 00:21:45,400
Have no fear.

392
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:47,897
My music has more than just soul.

393
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:49,240
It has true power.

394
00:21:49,660 --> 00:21:51,100
Are you insane?

395
00:21:51,340 --> 00:21:54,017
You think anyone's gonna
let you play another song?

396
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:58,747
You might not see it this way, but I'm
grateful for the time we spent together.

397
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:03,136
Thank you for these past two years,
and thank you for bringing me here.

398
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:06,854
My crew and I have rather
tragic memories of this place.

399
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:11,313
We lost an important battle here last
time, but we're ready to start anew.

400
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:13,886
I'm the musician of the crew.

401
00:22:13,980 --> 00:22:16,257
I may possess some
strength as a swordsman,

402
00:22:16,340 --> 00:22:18,869
but my job is to make
our journey more fun.

403
00:22:19,860 --> 00:22:21,213
I've heard the stories.

404
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:25,757
They think people are foolish enough
to believe that Straw Hat is dead.

405
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:26,877
Will you listen to me?

406
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:27,790
He's not!

407
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:31,224
Straw Hat Luffy is out
there, alive and kicking!

408
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:32,960
You can tell the world!

409
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:38,797
And while you're at it,

410
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:41,757
tell them he's going to be the
king of the pirates someday, too!

411
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:43,697
Boy, have I got some news for you guys!

412
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:45,477
We better print this one in a jiffy!

413
00:22:45,560 --> 00:22:48,617
Yeah, baby, he's coming back
soon, and when he sets sail,

414
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:51,347
Well, I want to send
him off Soul King style!

415
00:22:52,940 --> 00:22:54,080
That's so cool!

416
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:56,660
Do you love me down to my bones?

417
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:03,180
I'll dedicate this to
my crew, to my friends.

418
00:23:03,740 --> 00:23:06,220
My soul will sing to you one last time!

419
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:11,720
Luffy, let's go to the new world together.

420
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:13,300
The show is over!

421
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:14,837
I said you're under arrest!

422
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:15,979
Would you shut up?

423
00:23:18,260 --> 00:23:19,554
It's his last thought!

424
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:20,557
Let us hear it!

425
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,405
Please, what harm could it do?

426
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:23,330
She's right!

427
00:23:23,413 --> 00:23:26,162
You can wait till the show
is over, you bastards!

428
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:27,340
Music is power.

429
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:29,266
Music is always on your side.

430
00:23:32,020 --> 00:23:34,080
One, two, three, four.

431
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:37,760
I call this one New World.

432
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:46,737
This is Grove number 46 with an update.

433
00:23:46,820 --> 00:23:48,797
The pirates keep pouring in.

434
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:50,317
There's definitely over a hundred.

435
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:55,877
Now none of the main
Straw Hats are here yet.

436
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:58,960
But even so, I would approach
with extreme caution.

437
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:08,537
This is bad.

438
00:24:08,620 --> 00:24:10,237
Tell the backup they need to hurry.

439
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:13,917
Well now what have we here?

440
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:16,957
Who is this little fellow
whispering behind the rock?

441
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:18,957
Because he looks like a Navy soldier.

442
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:21,357
And my goodness what is this?

443
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:24,920
You weren't looking to crash
our harmless party, were you?

444
00:24:30,940 --> 00:24:31,817
No! No!

445
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:33,940
That's not very civil at all!

446
00:24:35,220 --> 00:24:37,677
Because if you were calling
your friends for backup,

447
00:24:37,760 --> 00:24:41,054
that would not end well,
seeing as they weren't invited.

448
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:43,817
Show some manners.

449
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:45,060
I saw him.

450
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:46,860
He was calling. No!

451
00:24:47,080 --> 00:24:50,857
I was going to call them, but I
hadn't gotten through them just yet.

452
00:24:50,940 --> 00:24:52,220
That is good to hear.

453
00:24:52,440 --> 00:24:54,440
And I say that for your sake, too.

454
00:24:55,220 --> 00:24:59,457
Because if your friends did show up,
this grove would be covered in blood.

455
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:00,560
Their blood.

456
00:25:00,780 --> 00:25:02,320
And your blood.

457
00:25:03,420 --> 00:25:04,820
Come on, Caribou.

458
00:25:05,020 --> 00:25:06,480
Back me up here. Huh?

459
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:07,677
I wasn't listening.

460
00:25:09,840 --> 00:25:11,777
Who do you think you're bowing to, moron?

461
00:25:11,860 --> 00:25:12,690
I'm over here.

462
00:25:14,260 --> 00:25:15,540
Please forgive me.

463
00:25:15,860 --> 00:25:17,680
You still can't get it right.

464
00:25:18,140 --> 00:25:20,200
What, are you blind or just stupid?

465
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:22,442
He's famous for killing Marines.

466
00:25:24,980 --> 00:25:26,300
Hmm? Hmm.

467
00:25:48,620 --> 00:25:50,900
Ah, do you think this is a joke?

468
00:25:51,500 --> 00:25:53,277
He really stabbed that guy.

469
00:25:53,360 --> 00:25:54,889
Then the stories are true.

470
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:58,860
Gods, have mercy!

471
00:25:59,260 --> 00:26:00,840
He is but a fool!

472
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:03,560
He grabbed his gun!

473
00:26:03,840 --> 00:26:07,980
This poor misguided soul tried
to incite violence against me!

474
00:26:08,340 --> 00:26:11,222
In your infinite kindness,
please show him mercy!

475
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:14,020
Sorry, gods. Sorry. Very sorry.

476
00:26:14,220 --> 00:26:15,060
Sorry, gods.

477
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:17,860
Now, brother, bury him.

478
00:26:18,100 --> 00:26:20,457
Bury this sinful transgressor alive.

479
00:26:20,540 --> 00:26:25,497
I dig so that his poor soul may
be free. Roger! Dig it! Dig it!

480
00:26:25,580 --> 00:26:26,420
Wait a second!

481
00:26:26,860 --> 00:26:29,566
What if I call them and
tell them not to come?

482
00:26:29,880 --> 00:26:31,409
That would be good, right?

483
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:33,540
That's enough, Caribou.

484
00:26:34,620 --> 00:26:35,450
Huh?

485
00:26:36,260 --> 00:26:38,680
You can bury that nobody later.

486
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:42,140
We got bigger fists to
fry right now. Yeah!

487
00:26:42,780 --> 00:26:45,157
Just tell us what you want
from us, Captain Loopy!

488
00:26:45,240 --> 00:26:46,299
We're ready to go!

489
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:49,717
Take a look around you, boys.

490
00:26:49,800 --> 00:26:53,917
This is history in the making you
probably don't know each other yet.

491
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:58,337
But you'll be Titus brothers soon
enough from here on out your straw.

492
00:26:58,420 --> 00:27:04,257
Not a bad deal and I swear

493
00:27:04,340 --> 00:27:05,497
when I become King of the

494
00:27:05,580 --> 00:27:08,521
Pirates you're gonna know
you made the right call!

495
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:14,157
But I need a promise from you first
cuz a real king needs loyal subjects

496
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:18,181
ones that will live and die for
him and wait on him hand and fight.

497
00:27:19,260 --> 00:27:24,897
Anything you say you're the man who escaped
Impel Down wrecked Eni's lobby stormed?

498
00:27:24,980 --> 00:27:27,156
Fruit Ford, and fought the Admirals!

499
00:27:27,360 --> 00:27:29,997
You've got the world government
quaking in its boots!

500
00:27:30,080 --> 00:27:33,139
Sailing the seas with you
is like a dream come true!

501
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:34,070
Listen,

502
00:27:34,153 --> 00:27:37,757
there's only one man fit to be king of
the pirates and he's standing right there!

503
00:27:37,840 --> 00:27:40,297
You get with him or you
get left in the dust!

504
00:27:40,380 --> 00:27:41,210
Yeah!

505
00:27:43,800 --> 00:27:45,660
Looks like the king's all here.

506
00:27:46,360 --> 00:27:47,500
Is this it?

507
00:27:48,100 --> 00:27:49,660
So where is everyone?

508
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:51,100
Stop making me wait!

509
00:27:55,480 --> 00:27:57,080
All right, enough!

510
00:27:59,620 --> 00:28:01,597
I didn't call you here at a party.

511
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,386
We got business to attend to.

512
00:28:03,580 --> 00:28:07,756
Some jackasses out there haven't been
showing me the respect I deserve.

513
00:28:07,940 --> 00:28:10,175
That is to say, they insulted my aunt.

514
00:28:13,620 --> 00:28:17,117
A red-haired girl, a long-nosed
guy, and a brat with a backpack!

515
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:18,797
Find him and bring him to me!

516
00:28:18,880 --> 00:28:21,939
The bastards are still in
the archipelago somewhere!

517
00:28:22,660 --> 00:28:24,200
Consider it done, boss!

518
00:28:24,420 --> 00:28:26,420
We'll make him suffer, you'll see!

519
00:28:28,800 --> 00:28:32,624
I gotta say, though, people sure
can't change a lot in two years.

520
00:28:32,740 --> 00:28:35,317
For one, you guys hardly
talk at all anymore.

521
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:37,237
He's more dangerous than we thought.

522
00:28:37,320 --> 00:28:40,037
We gotta get him to the boss pronto
or he's gonna rat us out to air.

523
00:28:40,120 --> 00:28:40,950
everyone.

524
00:28:41,033 --> 00:28:41,900
Who is this guy?

525
00:28:42,220 --> 00:28:46,197
I don't know, but in the meantime, let's
try not to talk so he doesn't catch on.

526
00:28:46,280 --> 00:28:47,177
The captain's right there.

527
00:28:47,260 --> 00:28:48,319
He can figure this

528
00:28:48,660 --> 00:28:49,490
out on his own.

529
00:28:49,573 --> 00:28:50,638
Sounds like a plan.

530
00:28:50,740 --> 00:28:51,637
I don't know what happened,

531
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:55,073
but it seems like you're
getting along a lot better, too.

532
00:28:55,660 --> 00:28:56,490
Yep.

533
00:28:56,573 --> 00:28:57,928
Time changes lots of stuff.

534
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:00,760
Like your faces, I mean.

535
00:29:00,920 --> 00:29:03,332
Unless you're wearing a disguise like me.

536
00:29:08,020 --> 00:29:09,549
Still not saying anything?

537
00:29:11,100 --> 00:29:13,100
The Navy? That's right.

538
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:18,237
They thought those fake Straw Hats were
the real deal and mobilized their forces.

539
00:29:18,320 --> 00:29:19,261
Pacifistas, too.

540
00:29:19,580 --> 00:29:22,580
I have them wiretapped, so
there's no mistaking it.

541
00:29:22,840 --> 00:29:23,670
Anyway,

542
00:29:23,753 --> 00:29:25,037
Brooke is finishing up his concert,

543
00:29:25,120 --> 00:29:27,977
but I gave him a call backstage
to let him know what was going on.

544
00:29:28,060 --> 00:29:30,837
He said he'd come after the
encore, so it shouldn't be long.

545
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:31,750
Oh yeah?

546
00:29:31,833 --> 00:29:34,074
Giving up stardom to be a lowly pirate?

547
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:36,497
Goes without saying, but
the man's got a backbone.

548
00:29:36,580 --> 00:29:37,600
All right, Nami.

549
00:29:37,860 --> 00:29:39,057
Since you're the navigator,

550
00:29:39,140 --> 00:29:43,397
there are a few tricks to operating
a coded ship I should pass on to you.

551
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:44,477
Uh, okay.

552
00:29:44,560 --> 00:29:45,736
Sure, let's hear it.

553
00:29:46,360 --> 00:29:48,417
We aren't getting ready
to take off, are we?

554
00:29:48,500 --> 00:29:50,317
We're still missing half the crew here.

555
00:29:50,400 --> 00:29:53,457
I mean, did Luffy even make
it to the archipelago yet?

556
00:29:53,540 --> 00:29:54,920
It's all under control.

557
00:29:56,860 --> 00:29:57,690
Captain! Huh?

558
00:29:57,773 --> 00:30:00,217
I'm kind of in the middle
of something, you goons.

559
00:30:00,300 --> 00:30:02,577
But we found a backpack
guy you was looking for.

560
00:30:02,660 --> 00:30:03,597
That's good, right?

561
00:30:03,680 --> 00:30:05,537
He's a friend of the crew, if you follow.

562
00:30:05,620 --> 00:30:06,640
Hello, say hi.

563
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:13,780
In other words, Luffy
arrived earlier this morning.

564
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:19,540
It's almost time to go.

565
00:30:19,740 --> 00:30:22,537
I gave Sanji a baby transponder
snail when he stopped by,

566
00:30:22,620 --> 00:30:23,717
so I'll tell him to come back.

567
00:30:23,800 --> 00:30:25,537
You should have Zoro with him, too.

568
00:30:25,620 --> 00:30:26,450
Good.

569
00:30:26,533 --> 00:30:27,363
We should hurry,

570
00:30:27,500 --> 00:30:31,735
because any moment now, the Navy will
be attacking with a sizable force.

571
00:30:32,180 --> 00:30:35,356
Unfortunately, there's no
way to contact your captain.

572
00:30:35,860 --> 00:30:39,497
But if you follow this Vivre card,
you should be able to hunt him down.

573
00:30:39,580 --> 00:30:41,897
Let's hope the fake straw
hats buy you a bit of time.

574
00:30:41,980 --> 00:30:45,197
Grove 42 is on the outskirts,
so it's close to the sea.

575
00:30:45,280 --> 00:30:48,677
Take the Sunny there and be ready
to depart on a moment's notice.

576
00:30:48,760 --> 00:30:51,677
I'm sure you'd like to relax
after these two difficult years,

577
00:30:51,760 --> 00:30:53,289
but it wasn't meant to be.

578
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:56,780
The winds of the new
world wait for no one.
